// Module c-autonomic: autonomic disorders for residents. Telling neurogenic from non-neurogenic
// orthostatic hypotension, central versus peripheral causes of autonomic failure, what each
// autonomic test shows, postural tachycardia syndrome and reflex syncope, and treatment
// principles (no doses). Pathways, Horner syndrome, bladder patterns, and the definition of
// orthostatic hypotension are taught in f-autonomic-pathways and are not repeated here.

