          body: "A 62-year-old engineer has felt faint on standing for a year and once blacked out in the shower. He also has constipation, erectile dysfunction, and urinary urgency with incomplete emptying. Over the same year his writing has become small and his right arm stiff. Levodopa helped a little at first and now seems to do nothing. His wife says he snores loudly and sometimes makes a high-pitched noise breathing in at night. He has been told he has Parkinson disease. Is that the whole story?",
